specs/hal-engine-chat-routes/spec.md:Returning the chat rather than a boolean is the same idea applied to the code: a guard that answers "may I?" leaves the caller free to carry on after a no, and that mistake is invisible in review. A guard that answers with the chat, or with nothing, makes carrying on a type error, so a route that forgets to stop fails to compile rather than serving an unauthorised chat.
